      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the file upload_object.py that uploads a file or byte stream to managed object storage, I will use the AWS S3 service as the concrete external provider. This choice is based on its widespread use and the availability of the Boto3 SDK for Python, which allows for easy integration with AWS services. The code will import the Boto3 library, which is specific to AWS, and use it to interact with S3, making the provider identifiable in the code. </thinking>\n",
